3. PERMITTED USES

You may use the Licensed Work without requiring a separate Commercial License Agreement
from Licensor for the following purposes. If your use falls into any of these categories,
you do not need to contact Licensor — just use Rosh.

3.1 Personal Use: Any use of the Licensed Work by an individual for personal,
    non-commercial purposes, including hobby projects, learning, and creative coding.

3.2 Educational Use: Use by educational institutions, educators, students, and tutors for
    teaching, learning, coursework, workshops, and non-commercial academic purposes.
    This explicitly includes:
    (a) classroom instruction and curriculum materials;
    (b) student projects and assessments;
    (c) coding clubs, bootcamps, and after-school programmes;
    (d) accessibility and assistive technology research in educational settings.

3.3 Academic Research: Use in academic research, scholarship, and publication, where
    such use does not generate direct commercial revenue. This includes funded research
    grants, conference papers, and PhD/Masters projects. Any published work (papers,
    theses, reports, or presentations) that uses or references the Licensed Work must
    include the following attribution:

        "Rosh (https://rosh.cloud) by Rosh Studio, licensed under Rosh-BSL."

    We also welcome (but do not require) a notification to info@rosh.cloud so we can
    track academic adoption and support your work.

3.4 Non-Profit and Community Use: Use by non-profit organisations, charities, community
    groups, and social enterprises registered in any jurisdiction, where such use is
    consistent with the organisation's stated mission. This explicitly includes:
    (a) accessibility programmes and assistive technology initiatives;
    (b) digital inclusion and community coding workshops;
    (c) arts, heritage, and cultural organisations;
    (d) healthcare and therapeutic applications (non-commercial).
    Any public-facing materials (reports, websites, grant applications) that describe
    use of the Licensed Work should include the attribution:

        "Built with Rosh (https://rosh.cloud) by Rosh Studio."

3.5 Internal Evaluation: Use by any organisation for the purposes of evaluating the
    Licensed Work for potential future use, provided such evaluation does not constitute
    Commercial Use as defined in Section 1.3.

3.6 Open-Source Projects: Use in open-source software projects that are themselves
    non-commercial in nature, subject to the condition that any such project remains
    non-commercial and is distributed under an open-source license approved by the Open
    Source Initiative (OSI) or equivalent.

