12. REMEDIES AND CURE PERIOD

12.1 Notice of Breach. If You materially breach this License, Licensor will provide You
     written notice specifying the breach and the steps required to cure it.

12.2 Cure Period. You have thirty (30) days from receipt of notice to cure any material
     breach. If You cure the breach within this period, Your rights under this License
     shall continue.

12.3 Incurable Breaches. If Your breach is incurable (such as unauthorised commercial
     use of the Rosh core, removal of license notices, or false branding of a fork as
     official Rosh), notice alone may result in immediate termination without a cure
     period.

12.4 Remedies. Licensor's remedies for breach include: termination of this License,
     injunctive relief, monetary damages, and recovery of attorneys' fees and costs.
     These remedies are cumulative and not exclusive.

